    ("incentive", "/ɪnˈsentɪv/", "/ɪnˈsentɪv/", "n. 激励，刺激，诱因，鼓励；adj. 激励的", "a thing that motivates or encourages one to do something", ["motivation", "stimulus", "inducement", "spur"], "Tracking your daily streak and watching the unfamiliar list shrink provides a strong incentive.", "追踪每日连胜天数并看着生词列表不断缩小，能提供强大的学习动力。", "词根：in(进入)+cent(唱歌)+ive → 奏起战歌鼓舞士气 → 激励，诱因", ["cet4", "cet6", "kaoyan", "academic"], 5),
    ("incorporate", "/ɪnˈkɔːpəreɪt/", "/ɪnˈkɔːrpəreɪt/", "v. 包含，吸收，把…并入；注册成立公司", "to take in or contain something as part of a whole; to include", ["integrate", "include", "embody", "assimilate"], "Voca incorporates the best design ideas from minimalist cards and Ebbinghaus planners.", "Voca 融合吸收了极简卡片与艾宾浩斯规划表的精华设计理念。", "词根：in(进入)+corpor(身体/整体)+ate → 并入同一个整体 → 纳入，包含", ["cet6", "kaoyan", "academic"], 5),
    ("indispensable", "/ˌɪndɪˈspensəbl/", "/ˌɪndɪˈspensəbl/", "adj. 不可或缺的，必不可少的，绝对必要的", "absolutely necessary; essential", ["essential", "vital", "crucial", "requisite"], "An accurate phonetic guide is an indispensable tool for self-taught learners.", "准确的音标指南是自学者不可或缺的工具。", "词根：in(不)+dispens(免除/省掉)+able → 绝不能省掉的 → 不可或缺的", ["cet4", "cet6", "kaoyan", "academic"], 5),
    ("inevitable", "/ɪnˈevɪtəbl/", "/ɪnˈevɪtəbl/", "adj. 不可避免的，必然发生的", "certain to happen; unavoidable", ["unavoidable", "inescapable", "inexorable", "certain"], "Forgetting is an inevitable biological process unless countered by spaced review.", "遗忘是不可避免的生理过程，除非通过间隔复习加以对抗。", "词根：in(不)+evit(避免)+able → 无法避免的 → 必然的", ["cet4", "cet6", "kaoyan", "academic"], 5),
    ("infer", "/ɪnˈfɜː(r)/", "/ɪnˈfɜːr/", "v. 推断，推论，推理", "to deduce or conclude information from evidence and reasoning rather than from explicit statements", ["deduce", "conclude", "surmise", "gather"], "Never infer unverified functionality without inspecting the actual artifact or documentation.", "在未检查实际文件或文档之前，切勿凭空推断未经证实的功能。", "词根：in(进入)+fer(带来) → 从已知事实带出结论 → 推断，推论", ["cet4", "cet6", "kaoyan", "academic"], 5),
    ("inherent", "/ɪnˈhɪərənt/", "/ɪnˈhɪrənt/", "adj. 内在的，固有的，与生俱来的", "existing in something as a permanent, essential, or characteristic attribute", ["intrinsic", "innate", "built-in", "inborn"], "Platform sandboxing has inherent constraints that must be documented transparently.", "平台沙箱具有固有的环境限制，必须透明如实地加以说明。", "词根：in(在里面)+her(粘附)+ent → 本身就粘附在里面的 → 固有的，内在的（常接 in）", ["cet6", "kaoyan", "academic"], 5),
