    ("perceive", "/pəˈsiːv/", "/pərˈsiːv/", "v. 感知，察觉，发觉；认为，理解为", "to become aware or conscious of something; to come to realize or understand", ["discern", "recognize", "view", "apprehend"], "Learners quickly perceive a boost in reading speed after mastering core high-frequency words.", "在掌握核心高频词后，学习者很快就能察觉到阅读速度的提升。", "词根：per(完全)+ceiv(抓/拿) → 通过感官完全捕捉到 → 感知，认为", ["cet4", "cet6", "kaoyan", "academic"], 5),
    ("perpetual", "/pəˈpetʃuəl/", "/pərˈpetʃuəl/", "adj. 永久的，永恒的；连绵不断的，没完没了的", "never ending or changing; occurring repeatedly; so frequent as to seem endless", ["eternal", "everlasting", "incessant", "continual"], "Without marking mastered words, learners often feel trapped in a perpetual loop of easy words.", "如果不剔除已掌握的熟词，学习者往往会感觉被困在简单词的无尽循环中。", "词根：per(从头到尾)+pet(追求/走)+ual → 一直走到底永不停息 → 永久的，不断的", ["cet6", "kaoyan", "academic"], 4),
