    ("prerequisite", "/ˌpriːˈrekwɪzɪt/", "/ˌpriːˈrekwɪzɪt/", "n. 先决条件，前提，必备条件；adj. 必备的", "a thing that is required as a prior condition for something else to happen or exist", ["precondition", "requirement", "necessity", "sine qua non"], "A solid foundation of 5,000 core words is a prerequisite for fluent academic reading.", "五千核心词汇的扎实基础是流利进行学术阅读的先决条件。", "词根：pre(预先)+requisit(要求/需要)+e → 预先需要具备的条件 → 先决条件", ["cet6", "kaoyan", "academic"], 5),
    ("pristine", "/ˈprɪstiːn/", "/ˈprɪstiːn/", "adj. 原始状态的，未受破坏的；崭新的，一尘不染的", "in its original condition; unspoiled; clean and fresh as if new", ["immaculate", "unspoiled", "untouched", "spotless"], "Restoring a word from the vocabulary book reverts its definition to the pristine dictionary text.", "将单词从生词本移除会将其释义恢复为词库原始的纯净文本。", "词根：prist(最初的)+ine → 保持最初完美状态的 → 一尘不染的，原始未受损的", ["kaoyan", "academic"], 4),
