    ("profound", "/prəˈfaʊnd/", "/prəˈfaʊnd/", "adj. 深远的，深刻的；渊博的，深奥的", "very great or intense; having or showing great knowledge or insight", ["deep", "far-reaching", "penetrating", "sagacious"], "Ebbinghaus's discovery had a profound impact on modern educational psychology.", "艾宾浩斯的发现对现代教育心理学产生了深远的影响。", "词根：pro(向前/到底)+found(底部) → 直达最深处的 → 深刻的，深远的", ["cet4", "cet6", "kaoyan", "academic"], 5),
